Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: limit association TTLM mapping to MLD peers

The SDK enables TTLM by default. A newly allocated station also has a
zero-initialized TTLM response status, which equals WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS.
Consequently a normal single-link association enters the TTLM mapping
helper. That helper iterates hapd->mld->links and crashes when the AP is
an independent EHT BSS without an MLD.

Require an MLD AP and an MLD station before applying negotiated link
mapping. Keep the existing enabled/status checks and explicit MLD path.
This is shared SDK behavior and does not depend on the device family.

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -5834,7 +5834,8 @@
 		p = hostapd_eid_channel_usage(hapd, p, buf + buflen - p);
 	}
 
-	if (hapd->conf->ttlm_enable && sta &&
+	if (hapd->conf->mld_ap && hapd->conf->ttlm_enable && sta &&
+	    sta->mld_info.mld_sta &&
 	    sta->mld_info.tid_map_info.ttlm_ongoing_negotiation_info.ttlm_resp_type ==
 	    WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS)
 		hostapd_apply_ttlm_mapping_to_driver(hapd, sta);
